back, so it prioritizes before Forced Deployment. There are 2 minions in play, so it flips to the Warlord side.</p><p>&gt; The Forced Deployment was TECHNICALLY in play befor the Warlord side came in effect, so it triggers first, moving the 9 minions to play.</p><p>&gt; Now the Warlord side is evaluated, there are 11 minions in play and the heroes lose.</p><p>The quirky question here is whether the card is a single card that came into play at the beginning of the game and subsequently ALWAYS takes priority regardless of whether it has flipped or not, or does it reset its priority when it flips as it becomes a new &#39;card&#39; at that time?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I&#39;m really curious about this one, because we FINALLY beat Voss tonight... if we played Situation 1 correctly. Situation 2 came as a hypothetical discussion that I thought was worth asking.</p>",
