        "raw": "<p>Yeah, you fully resolve the &quot;start phase&quot; actions on the villain character card (as that was in play before any other villain card) before moving on. So you resolve every &quot;start of turn&quot; thing on Voss&#39;s character card first - are there ten minions in play? Okay, he doesn&#39;t win. Next card - Forced Deployment, boom 10 minions are now in play. Start phase is over, move on to Play phase. You now have the remainder of the round to bring the minion count back down again. Otherwise, at the start of Voss&#39;s turn, you check his card and &quot;Are there ten minions in play? Yes. Bugger.&quot; ;).</p><p>As mentioned, a villain character card is still a villain character card, whether it flips or not. Once you&#39;ve resolved the Start Phase actions for that turn, it doesn&#39;t matter whether he flips or not - that phase is over and so his Start actions won&#39;t occur until the start of his next turn.</p>",
